@startuml
title Favorite Track — Interaction Sequence
actor "User Browser" as Browser
participant "Client UI (Next.js)" as UI
participant "Client Cache / Prefetch" as Cache
participant "Server Function (favorite)" as SF
participant "Prisma Client (lib/db.ts)" as Prisma
database "Postgres / SQLite (prisma)" as DB

Browser -> UI : Click "Favorite" (optimistic UI)
activate UI
UI -> SF : call Server Function /api/favorite (trackId)
activate SF
SF -> Prisma : upsert favorite (userId, trackId)
activate Prisma
Prisma -> DB : write favorite row
DB --> Prisma : OK
deactivate Prisma
Prisma --> SF : success
SF -> SF : updateTag("track:<id>")
SF --> UI : 200 OK (confirmed favorite)
deactivate SF
UI -> Cache : request revalidation / tag invalidation
note right of Cache
Server-side caches tied to cache-tags
are revalidated for affected routes
end note
Cache --> UI : new content on next navigation / re-fetch
Browser <-- UI : UI state reflects favorited status
deactivate UI

note over SF,UI
Optimistic update: UI may show favorited before server
response; server is source-of-truth and triggers
selective cache revalidation via updateTag.
end note

@enduml